  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 180°C (about 350°F).",
    "Lay the potato between two chopsticks or wooden spoon handles and cut slices about 1/4 inch apart across its length, stopping at the chopsticks so the base stays connected.",
    "Tuck the zucchini, eggplant, tomato, onion and basil into the slits, alternating so every few slits hold a different vegetable.",
    "Set the potato on a large square of parchment. Drizzle with the olive oil, season with the salt and pepper, and lay the herb sprig on top.",
    "Wrap the parchment tightly around the potato, set it on a baking sheet and bake 60 min, until a knife slides easily into the center.",
    "Unwrap and serve hot, with sour cream if you like."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Great with sour cream.",
    "Most hasselback recipes roast unwrapped at 425°F for 60 to 70 min for crisp edges; the parchment wrap and lower heat here steam the potato and vegetables soft instead."
  ],
